# Files that are tracked in git but are not this project's source code.
#
# Read by ripgrep (and anything else honouring `.ignore`), which is what Claude Code's Grep and
# Glob tools run underneath. `.gitignore` cannot do this job: these files are *committed*, so git
# has to keep seeing them and only the search tools should look away.
#
# Why it matters here: `zxing.min.js` is a single 336 KB line, `bootstrap.min.css` a single 232 KB
# one, and `mcp/vendor/ext_apps.js` 172 KB. One grep for a common word that happens to hit one of
# them returns that whole line as "context" -- tens of thousands of tokens of minified vendor
# code, in place of the answer. There are 16 such files.
#
# This hides them from *search*, not from reading. `rg --no-ignore`, and every path named
# explicitly (Read, cat, an import), still work exactly as before -- so the `export{...}` rewrite
# in ext_apps.js that `widgets._bundle` depends on is still one `--no-ignore` away.
#
# Keep this list in step with the `exclude:` block at the top of .pre-commit-config.yaml: both
# answer the same question, "which committed files did we not write?"

# Vendored third-party libraries, wherever they sit.
**/vendor/

# Minified builds, including the ones outside a vendor/ directory
# (auctions/static/js/Chart.min.js, auctions/static/css/print.min.css, bootstrap.min.css4).
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.min.css4
*.map

# Web fonts and images: binary, and grep can only ever produce noise from them.
*.woff
*.woff2
*.ttf
*.eot
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.ico
*.webp

# Deliberately NOT ignored, because they are ours and get searched on purpose:
#   auctions/data/aquarium_species.csv   the curated species vocabulary (41 KB)
#   auctions/fixtures/demo_data.json     the demo fixture (33 KB)
#   auctions/migrations/                 294 files, but they are the schema's history
#   *.svg                                red_tail_cat.svg etc. are hand-editable source
